apiSurface:
The library is consumed as a class instance:

```typescript
import { Stagehand } from "@browserbasehq/stagehand";

const stagehand = new Stagehand({
  env: "LOCAL" | "BROWSERBASE",
  model: "openai/gpt-4.1-mini", // or a model config object
  apiKey: "...", // for Browserbase
  verbose: 1,
  // Browserbase settings in BROWSERBASE mode
  // localBrowserLaunchOptions in LOCAL mode
});

await stagehand.init();

// Atomic actions
await stagehand.act("click on the login button");
await stagehand.act("type 'hello' in the search box");

// Structured extraction
const data = await stagehand.extract(
  "extract the price and title",
  z.object({
    price: z.string(),
    title: z.string(),
  }),
);

// DOM observation
const elements = await stagehand.observe("find all add-to-cart buttons");

// Multi-step agent (AISDK tools mode)
const agent = stagehand.agent({
  systemPrompt: "Do X and Y",
  mode: "hybrid", // "dom", "hybrid", or "cua"
});
await agent.execute("Navigate to GitHub and check the latest PR");

// CUA (Computer Use Agent) mode
const cuaAgent = stagehand.agent({ mode: "cua" });
await cuaAgent.execute("Search for laptops under $1000");

// Page access for raw Playwright
const page = stagehand.context.pages()[0];
await page.goto("https://example.com");
await stagehand.context.conn.send("Page.navigate", { url: "..." });
```

Key types exported: Stagehand (alias for V3), AgentProvider, modelToAgentProviderMap, LLMClient, V3Evaluator, connectToMCPServer, and various type exports for AgentTools, AgentExecuteCallbacks, eviction schemas, and trajectories.
